{{Lists of states and territories of India}}

These are lists of Indian [[States of India|states and union territories]] by their nominal gross state domestic product (GSDP). GSDP is the sum of all value added by industries within each state or union territory and serves as a counterpart to the national [[gross domestic product]] (GDP).<ref>{{cite web|title=Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP) at Current Prices (as on 31-05-2014)|url=http://planningcommission.nic.in/data/datatable/0306/table%20168.pdf|publisher=[[Planning Commission of India]]|archive-date=15 July 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140715140421/http://planningcommission.nic.in/data/datatable/0306/table%20168.pdf}}</ref> {{As of|2011}}, the [[Government of India|Government]] accounted for about 21% of the GDP followed by [[agriculture]] with 21% and corporate sector at 12%. The remaining 48% is sourced from small [[proprietorship]] and [[partnership]] companies, unorganized sector and households.<ref>{{cite web|title=National economic debate – Stock markets or rigged casinos – talk by Professor Dr. R. Vaidyanathan (IIM Bangalore) – 21 Jan 2011, Mumbai|url=http://www.youtube.com|publisher=National Economic Debates|access-date=1 November 2016}}</ref>

